    "updated_at": "2018-02-22T11:05:49Z",
    "body": "`<iframe>` last changed in 3784c5375a36e19373982984ff761b491125a5da, which fixes a regression.\r\n\r\nThe text for `<frame>` was introduced in a703b0f16cb6e0ef563511cb013a1de2f4b8b81d which suggests it was copied from `<iframe>`, but `<iframe>` said this in that very commit\r\n\r\n> When a Document in an iframe is marked as completely loaded, the user agent must synchronously run the iframe load event steps.\r\n\r\nso this seems like a bad case of copypasta.\r\n\r\nAt some point I'd like these two elements to share much more infrastructure in prose...",
